    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12318" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dănīsta</span></b> , ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δανειστής</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a money-lender,
			usurer</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fenerator (only in Plautus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Epid. 1, 1, 51</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 2, 67</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Most. 3,
				1, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ps. 1, 3, 53</span></i>; cf. Paul. ex
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 68, 14</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dănīstĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δανειστικός</span>, <i>money-lending,
			usurious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 3, 1, 129</span></i>
			.</div>
